  <h2>What we cover</h2>
  <p>SmartAbodeLab publishes explainers, practical guides, comparisons, and reviews across three core areas: smart-home automation, residential energy efficiency, and technology for urban homes and apartments.</p>

  <p>Our goal is to help readers make decisions with less hype and more context. We prioritize compatibility, reliability, privacy, energy impact, cost, long-term support, and the constraints that matter in real homes.</p>

  <h2>Who our content is for</h2>
  <p>We write primarily for readers in the United States and Europe, including homeowners, renters, apartment residents, and people building or improving connected-home systems.</p>

  <h2>How we build trust</h2>
  <p>Articles should identify who wrote them, show meaningful publication and update dates, distinguish research from first-hand testing, and link to relevant primary or authoritative sources where those sources materially support the article.</p>

  <p>When an article has been independently reviewed or fact checked, we identify the person responsible. We do not display those labels unless that work actually occurred.</p>

  <h2>Editorial independence</h2>
  <p>Advertising, sponsorship, affiliate relationships, and commercial considerations should not determine the conclusions of our editorial coverage. Any commercial relationship that could reasonably matter to a reader should be disclosed clearly.</p>

  <h2>Our standards</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><a href="/masthead">Masthead</a> — the writers and editors responsible for our coverage.</li>
    <li><a href="/editorial-policy">Editorial Policy</a> — how we research, write, review, update, and disclose content.</li>
    <li><a href="/review-methodology">Review Methodology</a> — how product reviews and hands-on evaluations should be performed.</li>
    <li><a href="/fact-checking-policy">Fact-Checking Policy</a> — how material claims are verified when an article is labeled fact checked.</li>
    <li><a href="/corrections-policy">Corrections Policy</a> — how substantive mistakes and updates are handled.</li>
    <li><a href="/affiliate-disclosure">Affiliate Disclosure</a> — how commercial links are separated from editorial judgment.</li>
  </ul>
